The GNU Boot project previously found nonfree microcode in the first=0ARC1 =
release (in gnuboot-0.1-rc1_src.tar.xz to be exact).=0A=0AThis was announce=
d in the "GNU Boot December 2023 News"=0A(https://lists.gnu.org/archive/htm=
l/gnuboot-announce/2023-12/msg00000.html).=0AIt=0Awas fixed by re-making th=
e affected tarball by hand with the nonfree=0Asoftware removed and by conta=
cting Canoeboot that had the same issue,=0Aand by bug reporting and proposi=
ng patches to fix the issue in Guix as=0Awell (they are still pending as we=
 need to find a reviewer familiar=0Awith Coreboot).=0A=0ABut recently we fo=
und a more problematic issue that also affects many=0Amore distributions an=
d all the previous GNU Boot release candidates.=0A=0AThe vboot source code =
used in Coreboot and in the vboot-utils package=0Aavailable in many GNU/Lin=
ux distributions contains nonfree code in=0Atheir test data in tests/futili=
ty/data (nonfree microcode, nonfree=0ABIOS, nonfree Management Engine firmw=
ares, etc).=0A=0ASo we had to re-release all the affected tarballs (like=0A=
gnuboot-0.1-rc1_src.tar.xz, gnuboot-0.1-rc2_src.tar.xz, etc).=0A=0AWe made =
and we improved the process along the way (we now store the=0Achanges in ta=
g inside our git repository and simply regenerate the=0Atarballs with the b=
uild system that is available for a given tag).=0A=0AWe are also in the pro=
cess of contacting distributions and/or=0Acoordinating with them and we als=
o need help as there are many=0Adistributions to contact.=0A=0ATo do that w=
e started contacting the free GNU/Linux distros=0A(https://www.gnu.org/dist=
ros/free-distros.html) that ship the vboot=0Asource code. We also contacted=
 Replicant that is a free Android distro=0Athat also ships vboot source cod=
e.=0A=0AWe also started to contact common distros that require certain=0Are=
positories to only have free software (so far we only contacted=0ADebian as=
 that will help Trisquel fix the issue, but we also need to=0Acontact Fedor=
a for instance). Finding which distro to contact is made=0Amuch easier than=
ks to GNU's review of common distros policies=0A(https://www.gnu.org/distro=
s/common-distros.html).=0A=0AWe coordinate that work on our bug report syst=
em at Savannah,=0Aespecially in the bug #66246=0A(https://savannah.gnu.org/=
bugs/index.php?66246).=0A=0A=0A____________________________________________=
